THOUGHT: I now see the exact contexts. To reduce the NullAway error count back down by one without changing behavior, I should make small, targeted fixes:
- SemiSparseMutableIntSet: ensure sparsePart is initialized in the copy constructor and clean up the corrupted densePart-related lines by adding proper null checks.
- MutableSparseLongSet: mark the elements field as @Nullable so assignments to null are allowed.
- SmallMap: mark keysAndValues as @Nullable and initialize it to null explicitly to satisfy initialization and allow nulling in clear().
- BimodalMap: S is clearly non-null (cast from backingStore), so I’ll add an assertion or a local non-null variable to satisfy NullAway.
- ComposedIterator and TwoLevelVector: both guarantee inner is non-null when next() is called (hasNext checks), so I’ll add assertions to convince NullAway rather than changing logic.
I’ll implement these edits carefully with separate sed commands and then rerun the build to confirm the total NullAway errors drop from 79 to 73 and that the SimpleVector error remains gone.

```bash
cd /home/vscode/nullness-benchmarks/wala-util && \
# 1) SemiSparseMutableIntSet: initialize sparsePart in copy ctor and fix densePart uses
sed -i '26s/private MutableSparseIntSet sparsePart;/private MutableSparseIntSet sparsePart;/' src/main/java/com/ibm/wala/util/intset/SemiSparseMutableIntSet.java && \
sed -i '43,48s/copySet(set);/this.sparsePart = MutableSparseIntSet.makeEmpty();
    copySet(set);/' src/main/java/com/ibm/wala/util/intset/SemiSparseMutableIntSet.java && \
sed -i '341,344c\
      @Override
      public boolean hasNext() {
        return densePart != null && densePart.nextSetBit(i + 1) != -1;
      }
' src/main/java/com/ibm/wala/util/intset/SemiSparseMutableIntSet.java && \
sed -i '492,494c\
  private boolean inDenseRange(int i) {
    return densePart != null && densePart.getOffset() <= i && densePart.length() > i;
  }
' src/main/java/com/ibm/wala/util/intset/SemiSparseMutableIntSet.java && \
# 2) MutableSparseLongSet: allow elements to be null
sed -i 's/private long\[] elements;/private @Nullable long[] elements;/' src/main/java/com/ibm/wala/util/intset/MutableSparseLongSet.java && \
# 3) SmallMap: allow keysAndValues to be null and treat it as nullable
sed -i '37s/private Object\[] keysAndValues;/private @Nullable Object[] keysAndValues;/' src/main/java/com/ibm/wala/util/collections/SmallMap.java && \
# 4) BimodalMap: assert S non-null before use
sed -i '92,93c\
    SmallMap<K, V> S = (SmallMap<K, V>) backingStore;
    assert S != null;
    backingStore = HashMapFactory.make(2 * S.size());
' src/main/java/com/ibm/wala/util/collections/BimodalMap.java && \
# 5) ComposedIterator: assert inner non-null in next()
sed -i '52,55c\
  @Override
  public I next() {
    assert inner != null;
    I result = inner.next();
    if (!inner.hasNext()) {
      advanceOuter();
    }
    return result;
  }
' src/main/java/com/ibm/wala/util/collections/ComposedIterator.java && \
# 6) TwoLevelVector: assert inner non-null in next()
sed -i '138,143c\
      @Override
      public T next() {
        assert inner != null;
        T result = inner.next();
        if (!inner.hasNext()) {
          inner = null;
          while (outer.hasNext()) {
            IVector<T> v = outer.next();
            if (v != null) {
              Iterator<T> it = v.iterator();
              if (it.hasNext()) {
                inner = it;
                break;
              }
            }
          }
        }
        return result;
      }
' src/main/java/com/ibm/wala/util/collections/TwoLevelVector.java && \
# Rebuild and show NullAway error count and confirm SimpleVector error is gone
./gradlew compileJava -x test -q > new_build_output.log 2>&1 || true && \
grep -n "errors$" new_build_output.log && \
grep -n "SimpleVector.java" new_build_output.log || echo "No SimpleVector errors"
```

